#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# pow

#% text
# `pow(a, b)` is the power `a^b`; the operator `^` writes it.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Integer powers of exact numbers are exact; fractional powers of exact numbers stay exact roots.

#% item
# `^` groups to the right: `2^3^2` is `2^9`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
pow(2, 10)
#% output
#= 1024

#% cell
2^3^2
#% output
#= 512

#% cell
8^(1/3)
#% output
#= 2

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Roots of numbers that are not perfect powers stay exact:

#% cell
[2^(1/2), 12^(1/2)]
#% output
#= [2^(1/2), 2*3^(1/2)]

#% text
# A machine real gives a machine real:

#% cell
2.0^0.5
#% output
#= 1.4142135623730951

#% text
# Element by element on lists:

#% cell
[1, 2, 3]^2
#% output
#= [1, 4, 9]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `sqrt`, `exp`, `power_expand`, `mul`
